WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.117
A global ORDER BY can be expensive in Spark because the entire result needs a coordinated order.

00:00:06.117 --> 00:00:08.987
That may be necessary for a final report.

00:00:08.987 --> 00:00:12.787
It is often unnecessary in intermediate transformations.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:16.787
Sort only when the order is part of the actual requirement.

00:00:16.787 --> 00:00:23.222
A shuffle moves data across executors so related keys end up together.

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:28.042
GROUP BY, large joins, and global ORDER BY can trigger expensive shuffles.

00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:34.717
In distributed systems, moving data is often more costly than evaluating the SQL expression itself,

00:00:34.717 --> 00:00:36.652
so plan around data movement.
